@prefix mem:      <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem#> .
@prefix prov:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dct:      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prof:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/dx/prof/> .
@prefix sh:       <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix wiki:     <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wiki#> .
@prefix wikirole: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole#> .

# ===========================================================================
# Proposal 03 — bring the 9 untyped affordance descriptors under the
# AffordanceDescriptorShape contract by typing them prof:ResourceDescriptor +
# wiki:QueryAffordance (from proposal 02) and adding the four required
# contract predicates: prof:hasRole, rdfs:label, dct:conformsTo, wiki:installedBy.
#
# Covers pod-audit findings descriptor:untyped @:
#   contact-find-by-name, contact-find-by-group, contact-find-by-email,
#   contact-find-by-affiliation, contact-find-by-orcid, org-find-by-ror,
#   org-find-by-name, bridge-card-to-wiki   (+ contact-find-by-affiliation listed twice in queue)
#
# DEPENDS ON proposal 02 (wiki:QueryAffordance + wikirole:query-affordance must
# crystallize first; this proposal cites both).
# ===========================================================================

<urn:uuid:7c1a0d20-5e44-4f3b-9a01-2026052303>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/meta/affordances/> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/meta/shapes/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-name.ttl> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:ProseDrift ;
    mem:rationale """Nine descriptors type only wiki:Affordance and so escape AffordanceDescriptorShape
(which sh:targetClass prof:ResourceDescriptor): no role/label/conformsTo/installedBy is enforced on them,
i.e. they work but are ungoverned. Resolved against the substrate shape (prov:used = /meta/shapes/,
specifically AffordanceDescriptorShape in shapes/substrate/affordance-descriptor.shacl.ttl) which lists
the four required predicates + the prose disjunction (sh:agentInstruction OR dct:description — all nine
already carry sh:agentInstruction, so prose is satisfied). Repair: add the missing contract predicates.
Each label/role is composed from what the descriptor already does (the selectQuery + its agentInstruction);
the role is wikirole:query-affordance and the type wiki:QueryAffordance, both NEW in proposal 02 (no
existing type/role fit — see that proposal's rationale). installedBy = the addressbook overlay (these
descriptors ship from overlays/addressbook/affordances/, confirmed in repo). conformsTo = the PROF spec,
matching every already-typed sibling (hub-view, breadcrumb-view, memento).

Two follow-on notes recorded for the reviewer (do not block this proposal):
 (a) FALSE-POSITIVE GUARD applied: I did NOT type these wiki:SearchAffordance even though that subtype
     superficially says 'query surface', because SearchAffordanceShape requires wiki:dispatchPattern +
     wiki:targetContainer which these client-run SELECTs lack — typing them so would FAIL SHACL. The
     misfit is the reason proposal 02 exists.
 (b) These descriptors use the absolute-URL subject form (</vault/meta/affordances/X.ttl>) rather than
     the relative <> form the typed siblings use. Harmless for the contract but inconsistent; the
     corrected overlay TTLs below keep the existing subject form to minimize the diff. Flag for a future
     style sweep, not repaired here.""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:34:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

# ===========================================================================
# Proposed change. PRIMARY repair is REPO-SIDE: edit the source TTLs under
# overlays/addressbook/affordances/ so `make reset` reproduces the governed
# form. (The deployed descriptor content could also be PATCHed, but the overlay
# is the durable home — a PATCH alone would be lost on the next reset.)
#
# For EACH descriptor, ADD these predicates to the existing subject. Shown as the
# block to insert; the existing `a wiki:Affordance`, sh:agentInstruction and
# wiki:selectQuery are kept (extend the type list to include the two new types).
# ===========================================================================

# Shared additions pattern (apply per descriptor, varying only rdfs:label):
#     a wiki:Affordance , wiki:QueryAffordance , prof:ResourceDescriptor ;
#     prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance ;
#     dct:conformsTo <http://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/> ;
#     wiki:installedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/overlay#addressbook> ;
#     rdfs:label "<see per-descriptor label below>" ;
#  (then the existing sh:agentInstruction + wiki:selectQuery unchanged)

# Per-descriptor rdfs:label (composed from each descriptor's own agentInstruction):
#   contact-find-by-name.ttl         "Contact lookup by full name"
#   contact-find-by-email.ttl        "Contact lookup by email"
#   contact-find-by-orcid.ttl        "Contact lookup by ORCID"
#   contact-find-by-affiliation.ttl  "Contact lookup by affiliation"
#   contact-find-by-group.ttl        "Contact lookup by group membership"
#   org-find-by-ror.ttl              "Organization lookup by ROR"
#   org-find-by-name.ttl             "Organization lookup by name"
#   bridge-card-to-wiki.ttl          "Card-to-wiki-page bridge lookup"

# --- Worked exemplar (the full corrected form of ONE descriptor, copy the
#     pattern for the other eight) -----------------------------------------
</vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-name.ttl>
    a wiki:Affordance , wiki:QueryAffordance , prof:ResourceDescriptor ;
    prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance ;
    dct:conformsTo <http://www.w3.org/TR/dx-prof/> ;
    wiki:installedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/overlay#addressbook> ;
    rdfs:label "Contact lookup by full name" ;
    sh:agentInstruction """
      Case-insensitive full-name lookup across all Person and Individual cards.
      Parameter: $name — a string fragment to match (e.g., "Wang Wei", "Smith").
      Returns all ?person IRIs whose vcard:fn contains the fragment (case-insensitive).
      Source: the aggregated contacts index at </vault/contacts/people.ttl>.
      Pass this URL as --default-graph-uri when invoking via solid-pod sparql
      (RQ-Pod-4 workaround for non-RDF resource traversal).
    """ ;
    wiki:selectQuery """
PREFIX vcard: <http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#>
SELECT ?person ?fn WHERE {
  ?person vcard:fn ?fn .
  FILTER(CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?fn)), LCASE(STR($name))))
}
    """ .
# (sh: prefix is <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#>, already declared in each source TTL's header.)

